# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit. Every script in this repo sources it if
# it exists, so your paths live in one file that is never committed:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required. Every value below is the default the scripts already
# use, so an empty `.env` behaves exactly like no `.env` at all -- set only the
# lines you actually need to change.
#
# Shell syntax, and written as `KEY="${KEY:-default}"` on purpose: the scripts
# source this with `set -a`, so a plain `KEY=value` would *overwrite* a value you
# exported on the command line. Written this way, `WORK=/scratch ./run_comfyui.sh`
# still wins over the file. Keep that form for anything you add.
#
# The nodes themselves read the TF_* runtime variables from the
# environment, and the launchers export them before starting ComfyUI, so setting
# them here reaches the nodes too.

# --- where things live -------------------------------------------------------

# The root under which ComfyUI, the venv and the caches are looked for. This is
# the one variable most people need: everything below defaults from it.
WORK="${WORK:-$HOME}"

# ComfyUI checkout. Must be the directory containing main.py / nodes.py.
COMFY_DIR="${COMFY_DIR:-$WORK/ComfyUI}"

# The venv that env/setup.sh builds and the launchers run ComfyUI from.
COMFY_VENV="${COMFY_VENV:-$WORK/.venvs/comfyui-tf}"

# TrajectoryForcing checkout -- the model code, imported rather than vendored so
# this extension tracks upstream instead of a stale copy of its math. Leave it
# unset and the extension looks next to itself, next to ComfyUI, and under
# $WORK; if it finds none it clones the pinned commit on first use.
# TF_REPO="${TF_REPO:-$WORK/TrajectoryForcing}"

# Interpreter env/setup.sh builds the venv with. Must be 3.11.
# PYTHON="${PYTHON:-/usr/bin/python3.11}"

# --- weights -----------------------------------------------------------------

# The RAE decoder. Defaults to $TF_REPO/checkpoints/rae, which is where
# TrajectoryForcing's own download script puts it -- point this at an existing
# copy rather than downloading a second 2 GB.
# TF_RAE_ROOT="${TF_RAE_ROOT:-$WORK/TrajectoryForcing/checkpoints/rae}"

# The flow checkpoint, if you want something other than the released TF_L_edit.
# The node's dropdown is the normal way to choose; these override the `auto`
# entry's download source.
# TF_CKPT_REPO="${TF_CKPT_REPO:-mervekocabas/TrajectoryForcing}"
# TF_CKPT_FILE="${TF_CKPT_FILE:-TF_L_edit.safetensors}"

# HuggingFace token, only if the checkpoint repo is gated for you.
# HF_TOKEN="${HF_TOKEN:-}"

# --- VRAM --------------------------------------------------------------------

# JAX preallocates nothing by default, which is what comfy.model_management can
# cope with. Setting this flips JAX to preallocating that fraction of the card
# and passes ComfyUI a matching --reserve-vram. Only worth it when sharing the
# GPU with a large torch model in the same graph.
# TF_XLA_MEM_FRACTION="${TF_XLA_MEM_FRACTION:-0.3}"

# Passed to ComfyUI as --reserve-vram when TF_XLA_MEM_FRACTION is not set.
# TF_RESERVE_VRAM="${TF_RESERVE_VRAM:-}"

# --- Slurm, for run_comfyui_slurm.sh and slurm/*.sbatch ----------------------
#
# These are the cluster-specific ones. The defaults are for the Tübingen ML
# Cloud's Ferranti partition and will not exist on your cluster -- check
# `sinfo -s` for partitions and `sacctmgr show qos format=name` for QOS names.

# TF_PARTITION="${TF_PARTITION:-h100-ferranti}"
# TF_QOS="${TF_QOS:-vs}"
# TF_TIME="${TF_TIME:-08:00:00}"

# Where the launchers keep their rolling logs (last 20 of each).
# TF_LOG_DIR="${TF_LOG_DIR:-<repo>/outputs/comfyui_logs}"
